#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dowel — a contract token: template fingerprint + bound holes + locus.

Mint once from path:line and a runtime instance. The token is not a pin
and not an invert query. Resolve later onto another tree answers two
questions together: where the template sits now, and whether the same
hole names still bind.

Seating uses the template's static parts plus locus (path, neighbors,
stem-split). Hole names are assayed after the seat is chosen — a clone
that kept the old names cannot steal a body that renamed them.
"""
